  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/1066674289/v0.24.0</id>
    <updated>2026-08-13T11:14:28Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ankimcp/anki-mcp-server/releases/tag/v0.24.0"/>
    <title>v0.24.0</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h2&gt;Fixes Claude Desktop&#39;s Code tab (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5132581753&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ankimcp/anki-mcp-server/issues/53&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;issue&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ankimcp/anki-mcp-server/issues/53/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ankimcp/anki-mcp-server/issues/53&quot;&gt;#53&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If every Anki tool call was failing with this, it&#39;s fixed:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto&quot; data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=&quot;Tool &#39;listDecks&#39; has an invalid outputSchema: JSON Schema declares an unsupported
dialect (&amp;quot;$schema&amp;quot;: &amp;quot;http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#&amp;quot;). The default
validator supports JSON Schema 2020-12 only&quot;&gt;&lt;pre class=&quot;notranslate&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Tool &#39;listDecks&#39; has an invalid outputSchema: JSON Schema declares an unsupported
dialect (&quot;$schema&quot;: &quot;http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#&quot;). The default
validator supports JSON Schema 2020-12 only
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Code tab validates the schema dialect; regular Desktop chat doesn&#39;t — which is why this only broke for some people, and only in one place. &lt;a href=&quot;https://modelcontextprotocol.io/seps/1613-establish-json-schema-2020-12-as-default-dialect-f&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;SEP-1613&lt;/a&gt; made JSON Schema 2020-12 the default, but MCP SDK 1.x hardcodes draft-07 with no way to opt out, so no setting on this server could have worked around it. The server now runs on the v2 SDK and emits 2020-12 for all 96 tool schemas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Upgrading:&lt;/strong&gt; reinstall the &lt;code&gt;.mcpb&lt;/code&gt; bundle below, or &lt;code&gt;npm i -g @ankimcp/anki-mcp-server@0.24.0&lt;/code&gt;. No configuration changes needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;g-emoji class=&quot;g-emoji&quot; alias=&quot;warning&quot;&gt;⚠️&lt;/g-emoji&gt; Removed: the &lt;code&gt;env://{name}&lt;/code&gt; resource&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This resource returned &lt;strong&gt;any environment variable&lt;/strong&gt; to the connected client with no allowlist. Over tunnel or &lt;code&gt;--ngrok&lt;/code&gt; that exposed your shell&#39;s environment to a remote party; as an MCPB extension it handed the model the &lt;code&gt;ANKI_CONNECT_API_KEY&lt;/code&gt; you&#39;d entered in Claude Desktop&#39;s settings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It was never documented and isn&#39;t in the bundle manifest, so almost certainly nothing you use — but if you did reference &lt;code&gt;env://&lt;/code&gt;, it now returns &quot;Unknown resource&quot;. The &lt;code&gt;system://info&lt;/code&gt; resource is unchanged and still reports &lt;code&gt;NODE_ENV&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Also fixed&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tunnel: responses could be delivered to the wrong client.&lt;/strong&gt; Requests were matched to replies using the client-chosen JSON-RPC id, which restarts at 1 on every connection. Two clients on one tunnel — or a single client reconnecting while a request was still in flight — could collide, causing one to receive the other&#39;s response and the other to hang for 25 seconds. Requests are now renumbered internally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consistent server version.&lt;/strong&gt; STDIO and HTTP reported &lt;code&gt;1.0.0&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;serverInfo&lt;/code&gt; while tunnel reported the real one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quieter startup.&lt;/strong&gt; HTTP mode no longer prints ~50 lines of controller registration on boot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Smaller install&lt;/strong&gt; — five unused OAuth-related dependencies removed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Under the hood&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Migrated to &lt;code&gt;@rekog/mcp-nest&lt;/code&gt; v2 and the v2 MCP SDK (&lt;code&gt;@modelcontextprotocol/{core,node,server}&lt;/code&gt;). This is a substantial internal re-platform, but &lt;strong&gt;no tool names, parameters, output schemas, or behavior changed&lt;/strong&gt; — 48 tools before, 48 tools after, verified across STDIO, HTTP and tunnel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One consequence worth knowing: &lt;strong&gt;tunnel mode serves the 2025 MCP protocol revision only&lt;/strong&gt;, while STDIO and HTTP serve both 2025 and 2026-07-28. A client that speaks only the newer revision now gets a clear protocol-version error over the tunnel instead of a confusing &quot;method not found&quot; — use STDIO or HTTP for those clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What&#39;s Changed&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;fix(deps): migrate to mcp-nest v2 + MCP SDK v2 — emit JSON Schema 2020-12 (v0.24.0) by &lt;a class=&quot;user-mention notranslate&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;user&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/users/anatoly314/hovercard&quot; data-octo-click=&quot;hovercard-link-click&quot; data-octo-dimensions=&quot;link_type:self&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/anatoly314&quot;&gt;@anatoly314&lt;/a&gt; in &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5140614156&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ankimcp/anki-mcp-server/issues/54&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ankimcp/anki-mcp-server/pull/54/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ankimcp/anki-mcp-server/pull/54&quot;&gt;#54&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Changelog&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;a class=&quot;commit-link&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ankimcp/anki-mcp-server/compare/v0.23.0...v0.24.0&quot;&gt;&lt;tt&gt;v0.23.0...v0.24.0&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
