  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Repository/1066674289/v0.22.1</id>
    <updated>2026-07-01T06:31:26Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ankimcp/anki-mcp-server/releases/tag/v0.22.1"/>
    <title>v0.22.1</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;h2&gt;Tunnel connection reliability&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This release hardens the tunnel client&#39;s behavior around expired credentials, so a stale token no longer wedges the connection or forces an unnecessary re-login.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Fixes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reconnect wedge fixed.&lt;/strong&gt; An authentication failure (close code &lt;code&gt;4003&lt;/code&gt;) that arrived &lt;em&gt;after&lt;/em&gt; the WebSocket opened but &lt;em&gt;before&lt;/em&gt; the tunnel was established never settled the pending connection. &lt;code&gt;connect()&lt;/code&gt; would hang, the internal &lt;code&gt;isConnecting&lt;/code&gt; guard stayed latched, and the token-refresh reconnect then failed with &lt;code&gt;connection_in_progress&lt;/code&gt; — leaving the client stuck until a full restart. Pre-established closes now reject the pending connection so the client recovers instead of wedging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Improvements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First-connect token refresh.&lt;/strong&gt; When the stored access token is expired but the refresh token is still valid, the very first &lt;code&gt;connect()&lt;/code&gt; now refreshes the token once and retries automatically — instead of failing and making you re-authenticate. Single-shot: a genuinely dead refresh token still fails fast with a clear re-login prompt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automatic re-login on session expiry.&lt;/strong&gt; In an interactive tunnel session (&lt;code&gt;ankimcp --tunnel&lt;/code&gt;), a &lt;code&gt;session_expired&lt;/code&gt; result now triggers the device-flow login automatically (prints the URL + code, opens the browser) and retries the connection once, rather than just printing an error and exiting. Gated to interactive (TTY) sessions and bounded to a single attempt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;No changes to the stdio or HTTP transports — this is tunnel-mode only.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What&#39;s Changed&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fix/tunnel first connect auth retry by &lt;a class=&quot;user-mention notranslate&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;user&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/users/anatoly314/hovercard&quot; data-octo-click=&quot;hovercard-link-click&quot; data-octo-dimensions=&quot;link_type:self&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/anatoly314&quot;&gt;@anatoly314&lt;/a&gt; in &lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;4783002946&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ankimcp/anki-mcp-server/issues/40&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ankimcp/anki-mcp-server/pull/40/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ankimcp/anki-mcp-server/pull/40&quot;&gt;#40&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
